  "description": "T1) Robinia: Remove to ground level.•Extensive decay and splits in the main stem.•Significant decline in the upper canopy since the previous survey (February 2024) •Significant dead wood throughout crown•Located over several gardensIn order to adhere to the Hackney Local Plan 2033 policy LP51, a replacement tree will be planted within the front or rear garden.&nbsp; The new tree will be at least light standard size (6-8 cm girth), a native species or one known to provide benefits to local wildlife, climate resilient, and a species which is not considered invasive in Hackney.&nbsp; The new tree will be planted during the next planting season, within 12 months of the removal of the existing one.",
